<title>GREECE: Natl Mortgage H1 profit up 7.0pct.</title>
<headline>Natl Mortgage H1 profit up 7.0pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Mortgage Bank of Greece said its first half pretax earnings rose 7.0 percent to 22.9 billion drachmas from 21.4 billion in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;The bank's profit growth was in line with management targets,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>National Mortgage Bank's profits would have been at least 2.0 billion drachmas higher had it not been for the new reserve requirement with the central bank that went into effect after June 1996, it said.</p>
</text>
